discovery:
Research Chapter {chapter_id} for {ruler} in {year} as candidate discovery only. Use the complete chapter guide and ten lenses below. Build a deduplicated pool of at least {candidate_target} unique relevant underlying documents across primary/legal records, institutional monitoring, scholarship, reputable reporting, local-language material, favorable and adverse interpretations, and contrary evidence. Search results are candidates, not evidence. Canonicalize URLs; exclude search pages, tag pages, snippets without recoverable URLs, irrelevant documents, mirrors, and syndications that add no content. Do not stop because the main narrative seems clear. If a per-turn tool ceiling prevents the target, return the largest verified pool and name the blocker. Number candidates {chapter_id}-C001 onward. For each give title, publisher, date, canonical URL, source type, language, likely exact lenses, one-line relevance, opened status, and duplicate-family note. Return query families, the complete candidate inventory, removals, source-family/lens matrix, inspection priorities, and gaps. Do not assign scores.

